    {
      "id": "5r98vnf",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Nutrition"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Nutrition encompasses the intake and biological processing of essential nutrients for growth, energy, and maintenance.",
        "The primary nutrients required by the human body include carbohydrates, proteins, fats, vitamins, and minerals.",
        "A balanced diet ensures the adequate intake of all essential nutrients in proper proportions to prevent metabolic disorders.",
        "Malnutrition and nutritional deficiencies lead to severe common nutrition disorders requiring medical and dietary intervention."
      ],
      "id": "wkxs3rt"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "opt51qo",
      "content": "• Nutrition is the process of obtaining food and utilizing it for energy and body functions."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yfg98cs",
      "content": "• It includes ingestion, digestion, absorption, assimilation and excretion."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cfvl2ss",
      "content": "• Good nutrition helps maintain physical and mental health."
    },
    {
      "id": "zgoktqw",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Steps in Nutrition"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dy2b1c5",
      "content": "• Ingestion – Taking food into the body."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pnusuwg",
      "content": "• Digestion – Breaking down complex food into simple molecules."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pm19uch",
      "content": "• Absorption – Nutrients enter the bloodstream through the intestine."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ae20848",
      "content": "• Assimilation – Nutrients used by cells for energy and growth."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "c3skqtb",
      "content": "• Egestion – Removal of undigested waste."
    },
    {
