    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Vitamin and mineral deficiency diseases (e.g., Scurvy, Rickets, Anemia, Goitre) are frequently tested in objective questions.",
        "Key distinction: Kwashiorkor is primarily caused by protein deficiency, whereas Marasmus results from severe total caloric and protein deficiency.",
        "Caloric values of biomolecules: Carbohydrates and Proteins yield approximately 4 kcal/g, while Fats yield 9 kcal/g."
      ],
      "id": "zqhq7jn"
    },
    {
      "id": "j049uia",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "12.Important Exam Points"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7mamlf8",
      "content": "• Carbohydrates are the main source of energy."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "061gyu9",
      "content": "• Proteins are body-building nutrients."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ee6cwag",
      "content": "• Vitamin D deficiency causes rickets."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mvpwepo",
      "content": "• Iron deficiency causes anemia."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gcykmz1",
      "content": "• Iodine deficiency causes goitre."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zkiisp9",
      "content": "• Protein deficiency causes kwashiorkor."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0iujnrg",
      "content": "• Vitamin C deficiency causes scurvy."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
